# All of these are OPTIONAL. The test suite runs with no env file at all:
# the mainnet fork falls back to a public RPC endpoint.
#
# Copy to `.env.test` (gitignored) if you want to override anything.
# The VITE_ prefix is required for Vitest to pick up the vars.

# Mainnet fork endpoint. The fallback (eth.drpc.org) serves historical state,
# which the suites need — they start several anvil instances over a few minutes,
# and an endpoint that prunes state quickly fails partway through. Point this at
# your own provider for faster, more reliable runs.
# VITE_ANVIL_MAINNET_FORK_ENDPOINT=https://eth-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/<your-key>

# Pin the fork to a fixed block, making runs deterministic.
#
# REQUIRES AN ARCHIVE ENDPOINT. Serving state at a past block is an archive
# request, and public RPCs refuse it — anvil then fails before genesis with
# "Archive requests require a personal token". Set this ONLY alongside an
# archive-capable VITE_ANVIL_MAINNET_FORK_ENDPOINT above.
#
# Note that anvil caches forked state in ~/.foundry/cache/rpc, so a machine that
# has already cached the block can pass while a clean checkout or CI fails.
#
# Pins also go stale: as the block recedes, providers prune it and the mainnet
# state the tests assert against drifts. The failure looks like unrelated test
# errors, not a bad block number. Refresh it periodically rather than setting
# it once.
# VITE_ANVIL_MAINNET_FORK_BLOCK_NUMBER=25835325

# Anvil's account #0 — a well-known key, safe to commit. Only used by tests.
# VITE_MAINNET_PRIVATE_KEY='0xac0974bec39a17e36ba4a6b4d238ff944bacb478cbed5efcae784d7bf4f2ff80'

# Only needed to regenerate ABIs via `pnpm wagmi generate`.
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# USE_VERBOSE_TESTS — detailed test diagnostics (quiet by default)
#
# This one does NOT belong in this file. It is read straight from process.env
# (no VITE_ prefix), and Vite only loads VITE_-prefixed vars, so setting it
# here has no effect. Pass it inline instead:
#
#   USE_VERBOSE_TESTS=true pnpm test
#
# Accepts "1" or "true".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
